From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Wed, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: recore: add the HDMI VBUS regulator (PG9) to U-Boot's DT

The kernel DT drives PG9 as a fixed regulator supplying HDMI VBUS
(reg_hdmi_vbus in sun50i-a64-recore.dtsi, wired to simplefb_hdmi via
vcc-hdmi-supply). U-Boot's DT had no equivalent node, so PG9 was never
asserted during U-Boot and the display stayed dark - confirmed on
hardware: setting it by hand with "gpio set PG9" from the U-Boot prompt
is what makes an image appear.

PG9 is not revision specific. It is defined once in the shared
sun50i-a64-recore.dtsi, which all of -a5/-a6/-a7/-a8 include, and no
per-revision DT overrides it - so this applies to every Recore.

This only works now that sunxi board_init() calls
regulators_enable_boot_on() (see
u-boot-sunxi64-legacy-3-regulators-enable-boot-on): U-Boot probes
devices lazily, so before that a regulator-always-on node would simply
have been ignored. It also has to come up before video probes and reads
EDID, which is why doing it via board_init() works where a manual
"gpio set" at the prompt is already too late to affect mode setting.

regulator-boot-on is included alongside regulator-always-on to match
the neighbouring usb1-vbus nodes in this file; regulator_autoset()
acts on either.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 arch/arm/dts/sun50i-a64-recore.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-a64-recore.dts b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-a64-recore.dts
@@ -101,6 +101,17 @@
 		regulator-boot-on;
 		enable-active-high;
 	};
+
+	reg_hdmi_vbus: hdmi-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "hdmi-vbus";
+		gpio = <&pio 6 9 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH> ; /* PG9 */
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
 };
 
